### eyeBridge API Test Collection
### REST Client for VS Code
### Install: REST Client extension by Huachao Mao

### ============================================
### VARIABLES
### ============================================
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001/api
@contentType = application/json

### Test User - Update email for each test run
@testEmail = testuser-{{$timestamp}}@eyebridge.test
@testPassword = TestPass123!
@testFirstName = John
@testLastName = Doe
@testPracticeName = Doe Eye Care
@testPhone = 555-0001

### ============================================
### AUTHENTICATION ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### 1. Register New User - SUCCESS
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}",
  "firstName": "{{testFirstName}}",
  "lastName": "{{testLastName}}",
  "practiceName": "{{testPracticeName}}",
  "phone": "{{testPhone}}"
}

### 2. Register with Minimal Data
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "minimal-{{$timestamp}}@eyebridge.test",
  "password": "MinPass456!",
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Smith"
}

### 3. Register - Duplicate Email (SHOULD FAIL)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": "AnotherPass123!",
  "firstName": "Duplicate",
  "lastName": "User"
}

### 4. Register - Invalid Email Format (SHOULD FAIL)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "notanemail",
  "password": "TestPass123!"
}

### 5. Register - Missing Email (SHOULD FAIL)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "password": "TestPass123!",
  "firstName": "John"
}

### 6. Register - Missing Password (SHOULD FAIL)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "test@eyebridge.test",
  "firstName": "John"
}

### 7. Register - Password Too Short (SHOULD FAIL)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "shortpass-{{$timestamp}}@eyebridge.test",
  "password": "S1!"
}

### 8. Register - Password Missing Uppercase (SHOULD FAIL)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "noupper-{{$timestamp}}@eyebridge.test",
  "password": "lowercase123!"
}

### 9. Register - Password Missing Lowercase (SHOULD FAIL)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "nolower-{{$timestamp}}@eyebridge.test",
  "password": "UPPERCASE123!"
}

### 10. Register - Password Missing Number (SHOULD FAIL)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "nonumber-{{$timestamp}}@eyebridge.test",
  "password": "NoNumbers!"
}

### 11. Register - Password Missing Special Character (SHOULD FAIL)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "nospecial-{{$timestamp}}@eyebridge.test",
  "password": "NoSpecial123"
}

### ============================================
### LOGIN ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### 12. Login - Valid Credentials (use email from registration)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

### 13. Login - Wrong Password (SHOULD FAIL)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "{{testEmail}}",
  "password": "WrongPassword123!"
}

### 14. Login - Non-existent User (SHOULD FAIL)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "nonexistent@eyebridge.test",
  "password": "SomePass123!"
}

### 15. Login - Missing Email (SHOULD FAIL)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "password": "SomePass123!"
}

### 16. Login - Missing Password (SHOULD FAIL)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "{{testEmail}}"
}

### ============================================
### TOKEN VERIFICATION ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### 17. Verify Valid Token
### INSTRUCTIONS: 
### 1. Run request #1 (Register) first
### 2. Copy the token from the response
### 3. Paste it in the Authorization header below (replace YOUR_TOKEN)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

### 18. Verify - No Token Provided (SHOULD FAIL)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify

### 19. Verify - Invalid Token Format (SHOULD FAIL)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify
Authorization: Bearer invalid.token.format

### 20. Verify - Missing Bearer Prefix (SHOULD FAIL)
### (Replace TOKEN with actual token from registration)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify
Authorization: YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

### ============================================
### USER PROFILE ENDPOINTS (requires valid token)
### ============================================

### 21. Get User Profile
### INSTRUCTIONS: Add valid token to Authorization header
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/profile
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

### 22. Update User Profile
### INSTRUCTIONS: Add valid token to Authorization header
PUT {{baseUrl}}/user/profile
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "firstName": "James",
  "lastName": "Johnson",
  "practiceName": "Johnson Eye Center",
  "phone": "555-1234"
}

### ============================================
### FAVORITES ENDPOINTS (requires valid token)
### ============================================

### 23. Get User Favorites
### INSTRUCTIONS: Add valid token to Authorization header
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/favorites
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

### 24. Add Favorite Vendor
### INSTRUCTIONS: Add valid token to Authorization header
POST {{baseUrl}}/user/favorites
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "vendorName": "Smith Vision Center"
}

### 25. Remove Favorite Vendor
### INSTRUCTIONS: Add valid token to Authorization header
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/user/favorites/Smith%20Vision%20Center
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

### ============================================
### HEALTH CHECK
### ============================================

### 26. Server Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### ============================================
### WORKFLOW TESTS (Full User Journey)
### ============================================

### WORKFLOW 1: Complete Registration and Login Flow
### Step 1: Register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "workflow-{{$timestamp}}@eyebridge.test",
  "password": "WorkFlow123!",
  "firstName": "Workflow",
  "lastName": "User"
}

### Step 2: Login (use email from Step 1)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "workflow-{{$timestamp}}@eyebridge.test",
  "password": "WorkFlow123!"
}

### Step 3: Verify Token (use token from Step 2)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN

### Step 4: Get Profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/profile
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN

### ============================================
### TIPS FOR USE
### ============================================
# 1. Click "Send Request" link above each request
# 2. Response appears in split panel on right
# 3. Use @variables for reusable values
# 4. {{$timestamp}} generates unique timestamp
# 5. Copy token from response and use in subsequent requests
# 6. Comment out tests you don't want to run with #

### ============================================
### POSTMAN NOTES
### ============================================
# If you prefer Postman:
# - POST http://localhost:3001/api/auth/register
# - Body: raw JSON (paste from requests above)
# - Headers: Content-Type: application/json
# - For auth endpoints: Add Authorization header with Bearer token

### ============================================
### COMMON ISSUES & FIXES
### ============================================
# 1. Connection refused (111)?
#    → Backend not running. Start: cd server && npm run dev
#
# 2. 400 Bad Request on register?
#    → Check password requirements (uppercase, lowercase, number, special char)
#    → Check email format is valid
#
# 3. 401 Unauthorized on protected endpoints?
#    → Token missing or invalid
#    → Make sure to use token from successful login/register
#
# 4. Database errors?
#    → Restart backend: kill server, npm run dev
#    → Or reset database if needed
